The name "XPlay" sounds catchy, modern, and easy to remember for Indian gamers, though you should watch out for trademark conflicts and avoid copying Sony's PlayStation UI too closely.
1. Name Feedback: "XPlay"
Pros: Short, punchy, and immediately communicates gaming. It looks great printed on a matte-black metal SSD enclosure or splash screen.
Trademark Risk: "XPlay" is an existing, well-known gaming brand name (originally the famous gaming TV show/media brand, plus several gaming accessories and software companies use variations of XPlay). Before spending money on packaging, domain names, or GST/trademark registration in India, check the IP India Trademark Public Search under Class 9 (computer hardware/software) and Class 28 (gaming consoles/controllers).
Safer Variations: If "XPlay" is already registered in India under Class 9/28, consider adding a unique prefix or suffix—like XPlay Deck, XPlay OS, XPlay Core, or XPlay Drive—to make trademark approval and domain availability much easier.
2. Customizing the PlayStation-Style UI
Using a PS5/PS4-inspired EmulationStation theme (like PS5ish or Art Book Next) gives a great console feel, but tweaking it to build your own identity is the right move:
Avoid Copyrighted Logos: Remove any official PlayStation icons, PS button prompts, or Sony startup chimes. Swap them for generic controller icons and your own custom XPlay boot splash video (/userdata/splash/) so your product looks like an original brand rather than a knockoff.
Signature Color Palette: Give XPlay its own visual identity—for example, a sleek matte black + electric cyan/amber accent instead of PlayStation's signature royal blue.
Custom Boot & Loading Screens: Replace the default Batocera loading screen and theme logo files with crisp vector graphics of your XPlay logo.
