which exact theme files to edit inside Batocera
To customize your PlayStation-style theme in Batocera and make it uniquely XPlay, you need to duplicate the theme folder so Batocera updates don't overwrite your work, and then edit specific XML and image files inside /userdata/themes/.
1. Copy & Rename the Theme Folder First
Access Your Files: Open Batocera's file manager (F1 on keyboard) or connect via SSH/SFTP from another PC.
Duplicate the Theme: Go to /userdata/themes/, copy your current PlayStation-style theme folder, and paste it with a new folder name like xplay-ui.
Never Edit /usr/share/emulationstation/themes/: That directory resets whenever Batocera updates. Always keep your custom theme inside /userdata/themes/.
2. Key Files & Folders to Edit
Inside your new /userdata/themes/xplay-ui/ folder, you will find a layout similar to this:
theme.xml (Main Configuration File)
What it controls: Global colors, fonts, default backgrounds, and overall screen layouts.
What to edit: Search for hex color codes (like #003791 or #0070D1 for PlayStation blue) and replace them with your signature XPlay hex color (such as #00F0FF for electric cyan or #FF9900 for neon amber).
Text & Labels: Look for <text> tags containing hardcoded names or welcome headers and change them to XPlay.
_inc/images/ or art/ Folder (Logos, Icons & Backgrounds)
What it controls: System logos, header banners, controller button prompts, and wallpapers.
What to edit:
Replace the main theme header logo (logo.png or logo.svg) with your XPlay logo using the exact same dimensions and file format.
Swap out any PlayStation-specific wallpaper files (bg.jpg or background.png) with your own clean dark/carbon background.
Replace PlayStation button icons (cross, circle, square, triangle or PS Home icons) with clean generic controller icons (A, B, X, Y) so buyers using Xbox, Cosmic Byte, or Redgear controllers aren't confused.
ports/ Folder (theme.xml and logo.svg/logo.png)
What it controls: How your Steam and Epic Games (Heroic) shortcuts look on the main home screen.
What to edit: Since you are putting Steam and Heroic inside /userdata/roms/ports/, edit the ports system folder inside your theme to give that category a custom banner and clean title like "PC Storefronts" or "Steam & Epic" instead of generic "Ports."
_inc/fonts/ Folder
What it controls: The typography across menus and game lists.
What to edit: Drop in modern .ttf font files (like Rajdhani, Montserrat, or Orbitron) and update the <fontPath> tags inside theme.xml to give the UI an instant custom brand feel.
_inc/sounds/ Folder
What it controls: Menu navigation clicks, selection chimes, and back-button sounds.
What to edit: Replace any recognizable PlayStation menu sound files (.wav or .ogg) with clean, subtle custom UI clicks so your drive sounds original.
3. Activate & Test Your Custom Theme
Select Theme: Press Start in Batocera, go to User Interface Settings > Theme Set, and pick xplay-ui.
Fast Reload Trick: While tweaking XML colors or image sizes, press Start > User Interface Settings > Theme Configuration or restart EmulationStation (Start > Quit > Restart EmulationStation) to see your edits in 2 seconds without rebooting the whole PC.
