whois privacy kya hai?
WHOIS Privacy (jise Domain Privacy Protection bhi kehte hain) ek security feature hai jo aapki personal details—jaise aapka poora naam, ghar/office ka address, phone number, aur email ID—ko internet par public hone se bachata hai.
Jab bhi koi insaan ek naya domain (jaise xplayconsole.com) kharidta hai, toh internet rules (ICANN) ke mutabik uski contact details ek public database (WHOIS Directory) mein save hoti hain.
1. Bina WHOIS Privacy Ke Kya Hota Hai?
Koi bhi stranger internet par jakar aapka domain search karega toh usko seedha aapka personal mobile number, email, aur Noida ka ghar ka address dikh jayega.
Domain kharidte hi agle 24 ghante ke andar aapko daily 20–30 spam calls aur fake emails aane lagte hain ("Sir website banwani hai?", "SEO karwana hai?").
2. WHOIS Privacy On Karne Par Kya Hota Hai?
Public database mein aapki asli details ki jagah registrar ki proxy details dikhti hain—jaise "Redacted for Privacy" ya registrar ka apna generic email/address.
Aap domain ke 100% asli malik (owner) rehte hain, bas aapki personal identity hidden rehti hai.
3. Iske Liye Paise Dene Chahiye Ya Nahi?
Bilkul Nahi: Cloudflare, Namecheap, Porkbun, aur Hostinger jaise achhe providers yeh feature 100% FREE (lifetime) dete hain.
Kahan Bachna Hai: GoDaddy aur kuch purane Indian registrars checkout par iske liye alag se ₹300–₹600/saal maangte hain—wahan se lene ki zaroorat nahi hai.
Ab jab domain aur privacy ka concept clear hai, kya aap chahte hain ki hum xplayconsole.com ke liye complete website landing page copy taiyar karein?




